<h2>4. Backend API Specifications & Data Contracts</h2>

<p>The FastAPI backend exposes clean, high-performance asynchronous endpoints:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 22%;">Endpoint</th>
      <th style="width: 10%;">Method</th>
      <th style="width: 28%;">Request Payload / Params</th>
      <th style="width: 40%;">Response Payload</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/query</code></td>
      <td><code>POST</code></td>
      <td><code>{"session_id": "...", "text": "...", "language": "en|hi|mr"}</code></td>
      <td><code>FinalDecisionOutput</code>: Structured answer, recommendation item, risk scores, waypoints, and evidence citations.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/analytics</code></td>
      <td><code>GET</code></td>
      <td><code>port_id=mumbai&period_days=7</code></td>
      <td>SST, Chlorophyll, Wave height time-series values, deltas, and Survey of India high/low tide predictions.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/pfz</code></td>
      <td><code>GET</code></td>
      <td><code>port_id=mumbai&radius_km=80</code></td>
      <td>List of active PFZ candidates with latitude, longitude, bearing, distance, SST, and Chlorophyll concentration.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/alerts</code></td>
      <td><code>GET</code></td>
      <td><code>port_id=mumbai</code></td>
      <td>Active marine warnings, risk levels (LOW, MODERATE, HIGH, CRITICAL), advisory text, and validity windows.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/navigation/route</code></td>
      <td><code>POST</code></td>
      <td><code>{"origin": {"lat": ..., "lon": ...}, "destination": {...}}</code></td>
      <td>Detailed passage plan: distance (km/nm), duration, waypoint coordinates, compass heading, and cell-by-cell risk.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/conversations</code></td>
      <td><code>GET/POST</code></td>
      <td><code>user_id=captain-uuid</code></td>
      <td>Array of conversation session objects with IDs, titles, and creation timestamps for chat drawer synchronization.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

